      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:05:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want to clarify some terms:\n* Flash page: a single erase chunk.\n* Flash bank: one or more contiguous flash pages, each with the same erase size.\n\nA flash device with uniform erase sectors has multiple pages, but just one bank, correct?\n\nThis code is returning the number of pages, but the number of banks is typically less than the number of pages.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "2ad6306c0b6c486926adb3bbe779894598b29b46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "578b7c29_38d1ef99",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:32:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Flash page: a single erase chunk\n\nYes\n\n\u003e Flash bank: one or more contiguous flash pages, each with the same erase size\n\nYes, it\u0027s also called `region`. Unfortunately, in EC codebase sometimes `bank` means `page` e.g. https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/flash.c;l\u003d167-189;drc\u003d3c5eb7bebec88813abb1a44a60230acdb05ef29e\n\n\u003e A flash device with uniform erase sectors has multiple pages, but just one bank, correct?\n\nCorrect.\n\n\u003e This code is returning the number of pages, but the number of banks is typically less than the number of pages.\n\nThat\u0027s right.",
      "parentUuid": "15764e2f_90f17859",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "2ad6306c0b6c486926adb3bbe779894598b29b46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62279ca5_04426012",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T16:06:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should this routine, and all the other `crec_flash_bank_*` routines return the bank/region instead the page provided by the Zephyr API?",
      "parentUuid": "578b7c29_38d1ef99",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "2ad6306c0b6c486926adb3bbe779894598b29b46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "947b4cce_8aa53e2c",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/flash.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 348,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T16:41:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. We can check implementation of these functions in common/flash.c, e.g. crec_flash_total_banks():\n\n```\nint crec_flash_total_banks(void)\n{\n\treturn PHYSICAL_BANKS;\n}\n```\n\nwhere PHYSICAL_BANKS is:\n\n```\n/* Number of physical flash banks */\n#define PHYSICAL_BANKS CONFIG_FLASH_MULTIPLE_REGION\n```\nwhen pages have different sizes\n\nor\n```\n/* Number of physical flash banks */\n#ifndef PHYSICAL_BANKS\n#define PHYSICAL_BANKS (CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES / CONFIG_FLASH_BANK_SIZE)\n```\nwhen pages have uniform size\n\n`CONFIG_FLASH_MULTIPLE_REGION` example (STM32F4)\n```\n#define CONFIG_FLASH_REGION_TYPE_COUNT 3\n#define CONFIG_FLASH_MULTIPLE_REGION \\\n\t(5 + (CONFIG_FLASH_SIZE_BYTES - SIZE_128KB) / SIZE_128KB)\n```\n4 first pages have 16KB size (64KB total)\n5th page has 64KB size\nOther pages have 128KB size\n\nSo there are 3 regions, but at least 5 pages.",
      "parentUuid": "62279ca5_04426012",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 348,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "2ad6306c0b6c486926adb3bbe779894598b29b46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
